# `@repo/{{ name }}-api`

Shared tRPC utilities for the matching Fastify service.

This package exports a small tRPC surface intended to be used by the generated service:

```ts
import { router, publicProcedure } from "@repo/{{ name }}-api";

const api = router({
	// use `publicProcedure` to build routes shared with the service
});
```

When you generate a Fastify service called `foo` the generator creates `packages/foo-api` and
publishes it locally as `@repo/foo-api`. The generated service imports from that package so your
service and package remain decoupled at development time.

Add it to a workspace in the usual way (the generator already places it under `packages/`):

```bash
npm install @repo/{{ name }}-api -w <workspace>
```

## Scripts

- `test` — `vitest run`
- `test:watch` — `vitest`
- `test:coverage` — `vitest run --coverage`
- `check-types` — `tsc`

Run them from the repo root, or with Turbo: `npx turbo run test --filter=@repo/{{ packageName }}`.

## Boundaries

`turbo.json` tags this workspace `["{{ tag }}"]`. The package's `tsconfig` and tag enforce what it may
depend on (see `@repo/typescript-config` for details).

{{#if isBrowser}}
This package targets the browser; it extends `@repo/typescript-config/react.json`.
{{else if isNode}}
This package targets Node; it extends `@repo/typescript-config/node.json`.
{{else}}
This package is isomorphic; it extends `@repo/typescript-config/library.json` and avoids Node-only
APIs so it can be used by both client and server code.
{{/if}}

## Exports

Public surface is exported from `src/index.ts`. Keep public symbols small and tag intended exports
`@public` so `knip` does not report them as unused.
